        <mxCell id="rJWZjPf2SnsjCbNWOLVo-21" value="&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;keep Interview panel ready&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;keep bar raise rules ready&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;feedback should be available after every round&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;must have, good to have, least to have&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="255" y="840" width="265" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rJWZjPf2SnsjCbNWOLVo-24" value="When executing sourcing and recruitment, I treat talent acquisition as a precision funnel rather than a numbers game&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,1&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,2&quot;&gt;. I start with a deep intake session with recruiters to calibrate must-have outcomes over generic requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,3&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,4&quot;&gt;. By diversifying across outbound sourcing, employee referrals, and engineering branding, I build an active, balanced talent pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,5&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,6&quot;&gt;. I monitor stage conversion metrics daily to keep candidate velocity high and time-in-stage low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,7&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;27,0,8&quot;&gt;.&quot;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
