        <mxCell id="rJWZjPf2SnsjCbNWOLVo-62" value="Wrong hire and raise incident" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="820" y="810" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rJWZjPf2SnsjCbNWOLVo-67" value="I leverage &lt;b data-index-in-node=&quot;12&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,0&quot;&gt;DORA metrics&lt;/b&gt; as both engineering velocity indicators and key health signals for team onboarding and performance&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,1&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,2&quot;&gt;. During onboarding, I track an engineer&#39;s &lt;b data-index-in-node=&quot;43&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,2&quot;&gt;Deployment Frequency&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b data-index-in-node=&quot;68&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,2&quot;&gt;Lead Time for Changes&lt;/b&gt; against our team baseline to measure their 30-60-90 day ramp velocity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,3&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,4&quot;&gt;. If a new hire&#39;s lead time is lagging, it flags pipeline friction, access issues, or a code review bottleneck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,5&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,6&quot;&gt;. Across the broader team, spikes in &lt;b data-index-in-node=&quot;37&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,6&quot;&gt;Change Failure Rate&lt;/b&gt; signal burnout or tech debt, allowing me to adjust workloads proactively before it impacts retention&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,7&quot;&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;superscript&quot;&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0,8&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="645" y="880" width="400" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
